/ActualText (ANALOGY \057 A capable assistant in a well\055run workplace Imagine hiring an assistant who can read quickly\054 explain unfamiliar material and suggest a useful next step\056 You would still give that person a defined role\054 access to the right records\054 a spending limit and a way to ask for approval\056 You would record important decisions and check that promised work actually happened\056 The assistant\047s talent would not replace those arrangements\056 An agent system needs the same separation of responsibilities\056 The model supplies useful judgment\055shaped proposals\056 Your software supplies the records\054 rules\054 tools and checks\056 Where it stops\072 a model does not become a responsible employee merely because its language sounds human\056 Its apparent confidence is not evidence of permission\054 accuracy or successful execution\056)
>>
endobj
