/Alt (VISUAL LAB 1C \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 Two retry owners can multiply one request\056 ShopAssist requests one model response\056 Every network attempt fails with a retryable error\056 Compare four constructed configurations\073 each cap includes the first attempt\054 and the deadline permits every listed attempt\056\056 0\056 9 network attempts\056 Application 1 x adapter 1\056 1 network attempts\056 Application 3 x adapter 1\056 3 network attempts\056 Application 1 x adapter 3\056 3 network attempts\056 Application 3 x adapter 3\056 9 network attempts\056 Worst\055case attempts \075 application cap x adapter cap\073 successful earlier calls stop retrying\056\056 Each application attempt starts a fresh adapter attempt allowance\056\056 Both layers owning three attempts permits nine requests to the failing provider\056\056 One retry owner keeps the total allowance explicit\056\056 PREDICT\056 With the adapter capped at 3 attempts\054 what application cap reduces the worst case from 9 to 3\077\056 Count retries across the whole call stack\054 not one loop at a time\056\056 Constructed worst case\072 serial attempts\054 persistent retryable failures\054 no hidden retries and enough deadline\056 Counts are attempts\054 not extra retries\056\056 Check your prediction\056 R01 \057 AWS\072 timeouts\054 retries and jitter)
