/ActualText (ANALOGY \057 A taxi with a destination and operating rules A taxi passenger chooses a destination\054 while the driver chooses turns using current traffic and road conditions\056 A fixed train route chooses the path in advance\056 The taxi company still sets operating rules\072 licensed driver\054 permitted area\054 fare limits and a way to stop the journey\056 An agent resembles the taxi when discoveries change its route\073 a workflow resembles the train when known steps determine the path\056 Where it stops\072 software authorization must be enforced before actions\054 and a model is not a licensed person exercising accountable professional judgment\056 A driver analogy does not prove that a generated decision is safe\056)
