/ActualText (ANALOGY \057 The service counter and the back office At a government service office\054 a sign tells applicants which counter handles renewals and a form specifies the required fields\056 Behind the counter\054 staff check identity\054 eligibility and records before issuing a document\056 An application receipt identifies the work so a caller can ask about its status without submitting a second application\056 Where it stops\072 a receipt alone cannot force another office to avoid duplicate work\056 Software retries and uncertain external effects need atomic records or an explicit downstream idempotency\057reconciliation contract\056)
