/Alt (VISUAL LAB 7A \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 The handover keeps the same intent\056 A worker saves K\05517\054 submits the refund\054 then crashes before saving a result\056 Its replacement reconciles the retained intent\056\056 09\07240 saved\056 Accepted intent persisted\056 intent\056 K\05517\056 receipt\056 none recorded\056 status\056 pending submission\056 09\07242 resumed\056 No durable result after crash\056 intent\056 K\05517\056 receipt\056 none recorded\056 status\056 outcome unknown\056 09\07243 reconciled\056 Provider confirms original refund\056 intent\056 K\05517\056 receipt\056 RF\0559 confirmed\056 status\056 effect confirmed\056 K\05517 always identifies the same accepted payment\054 currency and amount\056\056 Green edge \075 changed field\073 gray \075 retained field\056\056 The intent is durable before submission\056\056 Missing local receipt means uncertainty\054 not proof of no refund\056\056 Reconciliation adds outcome evidence without creating another business intent\056\056 PREDICT\056 If the provider cannot resolve K\05517\054 which cells may safely change to confirmed\077\056 A saved intent tells a new worker what to reconcile\054 not what to repeat\056\056 Fictional record projection\073 provider status resolves K\05517 here\056 The handover analogy does not provide exclusive ownership or external atomicity\056\056 Check your prediction)
>>
