/Alt (VISUAL LAB 7C \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 Replay an event once\054 even when delivered twice\056 Snapshot E20 retains 8 unused model turns\056 Rebuilding the projection receives accounting events E21\054 E22\054 duplicate E22\054 and E23\056 Each unique event represents one already completed generation\073 replay invokes no model\056\056 AVAILABLE AT START\056 8 model turns left\056 EVENT \057 CHANGE\056 BALANCE AFTER EVENT\056 E21\072 first delivery\056 \0551\056 7 model turns left\056 E22\072 first delivery\056 \0551\056 6 model turns left\056 E22\072 duplicate delivery ignored\056 \0530\056 6 model turns left\056 E23\072 first delivery\056 \0551\056 5 model turns left\056 Persist cursor and debit together\056 Replay restores settled usage\073 it reserves no new calls\056\056 The snapshot already incorporates all accounting through E20\056\056 A repeated event identity describes the same generation\054 not additional work\056\056 Three unique events reduce 8 remaining turns to 5\056\056 PREDICT\056 If E22 arrives a third time after E23\054 should the remaining allowance fall from 5 to 4\077\056 An accounting projection counts accepted event identities\054 not delivery attempts\056\056 Constructed ordered event stream and atomic projection\057cursor commit\056 Turns were settled at generation\073 replay adds no reservation\054 model call or external effect\056\056 Check your prediction\056 R07 \057 Microsoft\072 event replay and idempotency)
>>
