/P 3329 0 R
/Pg 607 0 R
/K 0
/Alt (VISUAL LAB 11C \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 A valid balance can conceal a torn effect record\056 A deliberately broken payment test fixture commits its refunded balance but omits the key receipt\056 The shipped companion instead commits both atomically\056 These constructed records describe a contract defect to detect\056\056 Broken fixture PAY\055B\056 captured\056 2499 INR minor units\056 refunded\056 2499 INR minor units\056 accepted key\056 K\05517\056 key receipt\056 missing\056 Balance range\056 PASS\056 0 \074\075 refunded \074\075 captured\056 Effect attribution\056 FAIL\056 K\05517 has no retained matching receipt\056 Verified recovery\056 WAIT\056 Cannot prove the submitted operation result\056 Fail the service contract test\073 retain uncertainty\056\056 The balance passes its local numeric invariant\056\056 The missing key receipt breaks the promised attribution and recovery contract\056\056 A correct fixture commits balance and key result in the same transaction\056\056 PREDICT\056 Does the passing balance check alone establish that K\05517 can be recovered correctly\077\056 Verify the complete transaction invariant\054 including the evidence needed for recovery\056\056 Constructed broken fixture\054 not a reported test run\056 Correct SQLite transaction behavior depends on its supported storage and durability assumptions\073 databases remain separate\056\056 Check your prediction\056 R11 \057 SQLite\072 atomic commit and crash testing)
>>
endobj
