/Alt (VISUAL LAB 12A \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 Three real pages\054 three different relationships\056 A customer asks whether a used blender can be returned\056 All three evidence IDs exist\054 are current\054 and are permitted for this customer\056\056 CLAIMS\056 PASSAGES\056 C1\056 Unused blenders qualify for returns within 30 days\056\056 E1\056 Returns v3\054 section 2\072 unused blenders may be returned within 30 days\056\056 C2\056 Used blenders qualify for ordinary returns within 30 days\056\056 E2\056 Returns v3\054 section 2\072 used items are excluded\073 faulty items use warranty\056\056 C3\056 The warranty guarantees a full refund tomorrow\056\056 E3\056 Warranty v2\054 section 4\072 submit fault details for assessment and remedy\056\056 SUPPORTS\056 CONFLICTS\056 INSUFFICIENT\056 Explain the used\055item exclusion\073 assess faults without promising a remedy\056\056 Every ID is valid\054 so identifier membership alone accepts all three\056\056 The ordinary return rule explicitly excludes the used item\056\056 Warranty assessment does not establish either refund amount or arrival time\056\056 PREDICT\056 If all three claims carry valid IDs\054 which claims may be published unchanged under this evidence\077\056 A real citation is inspectable evidence\054 not automatic support for its attached claim\056\056 Fictional policy excerpts\073 the exam analogy does not guarantee correct interpretation\056 Semantic judgments are explicit here\054 not measured verifier performance\056\056 Check your prediction)
>>
