/Alt (VISUAL LAB 12B \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 Rates need the right denominator and uncertainty\056 Constructed evaluation counts illustrate four different checks\056 Treat each row as independent Bernoulli trials within its stated population\073 these are teaching data\054 not measured system results\056\056 0\045\056 25\045\056 50\045\056 75\045\056 100\045\056 Answerable\072 retrieval hit\056 Count\072 32 \057 40\056 80\0560\045 \13365\0562\045\054 89\0565\045\135\056 Citation IDs valid\056 Count\072 40 \057 40\056 100\0560\045 \13391\0562\045\054 100\0560\045\135\056 Cited claims supported\056 Count\072 28 \057 40\056 70\0560\045 \13354\0566\045\054 81\0569\045\135\056 Unanswerable\072 abstained\056 Count\072 17 \057 20\056 85\0560\045 \13364\0560\045\054 94\0568\045\135\056 Constructed counts\073 two\055sided 95\045 Wilson intervals\054 z \075 1\05696\073 distinct populations\056\056 Retrieval hit means at least one relevant item\054 not full relevant\055set recall\056\056 Valid IDs can coexist with a much lower claim\055support rate\056\056 Unanswerable questions use abstention\054 not a zero\055denominator recall calculation\056\056 PREDICT\056 Does 40 valid citation IDs out of 40 prove every cited claim is supported\077\056 Measure the property you need\054 name its denominator\054 and retain statistical uncertainty\056\056 Constructed independent\055trial illustration\073 Wilson uses z \075 1\05696\056 Real clustered queries or repeated runs need dependence\055aware analysis\056\056 Check your prediction)
>>
endobj
