/Alt (VISUAL LAB 12C \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 Fuse ranks without pretending scores share units\056 Two authorized current\055source searches use different raw\055score scales\056 Fuse their ranks with constant 1\054 then multiply every fused score by 12 so the arithmetic is visible\056 These lists are constructed\056\056 0\056 10 12 x RRF score\056 B\072 lexical 2\054 dense 1\056 10 12 x RRF score\056 A\072 lexical 1\054 dense 3\056 9 12 x RRF score\056 D\072 dense 2 only\056 4 12 x RRF score\056 C\072 lexical 3 only\056 3 12 x RRF score\056 Lists\072 lexical A\054B\054C\073 dense B\054D\054A\056 Sum 12 \057 \0501 \053 rank\051\073 absence contributes 0\056\056 B receives 12 \057 3 \053 12 \057 2 \075 10\056\056 A receives 12 \057 2 \053 12 \057 4 \075 9\056\056 The numbers encode rank agreement\054 not factual support or calibrated relevance\056\056 PREDICT\056 If the dense list contributes nothing\054 which document ranks first and what is its displayed score\077\056 Rank fusion combines ordered evidence without equating the original retrieval scores\056\056 Constructed unique document lists with identical access filters\073 one\055based ranks\054 constant 1 and display multiplier 12\056 Scores are not measured quality\056\056 Check your prediction\056 R12 \057 Elastic\072 reciprocal rank fusion)
>>
