/Alt (VISUAL LAB 13C \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 A useful search hypothesis is still not evidence\056 AegisOps generates H1 to improve an incident search\072 perhaps the connection pool was exhausted\056 Authorized retrieval then returns metrics and sampled traces\056 Inspect which claims the actual records support\056\056 CLAIMS\056 PASSAGES\056 C1\056 Pool exhaustion caused the checkout slowdown\056\056 H1\056 Generated search draft guesses pool exhaustion\073 it contains no observations\056\056 C2\056 Recorded pool use peaked at 40 of 100 connections\056\056 E1\056 Metrics M\0558\054 10\07200\05510\07210\072 maximum connections 40\073 configured limit 100\056\056 C3\056 All sampled requests waited for a pool slot\056\056 E2\056 Trace T\0559\054 same window\072 0 of 20 sampled requests waited for a pool slot\056\056 INSUFFICIENT\056 SUPPORTS\056 CONFLICTS\056 Retain C2\073 reject C3\073 keep the causal question unresolved without citing H1\056\056 H1 influences where to search but cannot substantiate the guessed explanation\056\056 E1 supports a bounded observation about the displayed metric window\056\056 E2 contradicts the claim about these sampled requests\054 not every possible request\056\056 PREDICT\056 May H1 support the causal conclusion merely because it helped retrieve E1 and E2\077\056 Generated search text can guide discovery without becoming a source for factual claims\056\056 Fictional records and samples for the stated window\073 no conclusion about unsampled requests\056 HyDE is a search aid\054 and causation remains unresolved\056\056 Check your prediction\056 R13 \057 HyDE\072 hypothetical documents for retrieval)
