/ActualText (ANALOGY \057 Standard connectors and a company equipment register A standard connector lets a laptop recognize different approved devices without a custom cable for each one\056 The company\047s equipment register still decides which devices may connect\054 what software they require and who may use them\056 A network printer additionally has its own access and operating rules\056 Where it stops\072 a shared connector does not make a device trustworthy or interoperable in every feature\056 MCP peers need compatible protocol\057transport\057authentication contracts\054 and a server\047s description or annotation cannot grant itself permission\056)
>>
endobj
