/Alt (VISUAL LAB 20A \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 Three permission ceilings must overlap\056 Priya asks the refunds workload to act on an order\056 These constructed cases vary user entitlement\054 workload authority and the current task scope independently\056\056 User entitled\056 Workload allowed\056 Task in scope\056 O\055481\072 scoped refund\056 ALLOW\056 ALLOW\056 ALLOW\056 O\055902\072 other tenant\056 DENY\056 ALLOW\056 ALLOW\056 O\055481\072 reader workload\056 ALLOW\056 DENY\056 ALLOW\056 O\055481\072 status\055only task\056 ALLOW\056 ALLOW\056 DENY\056 All three must allow\073 approval\054 credential and downstream financial checks still apply\056\056 Compare each row with the scoped\055refund baseline\056\056 A single denial defeats the intersection even when the other two columns allow\056\056 The first row passes these ceilings\054 not every execution requirement\056\056 PREDICT\056 Can the refunds workload compensate for Priya lacking access to O\055902\077\056 Intersect authority\073 never combine privileges to bypass a denial\056\056 Fictional user\055directed cases\073 background jobs use a separate reviewed workload policy\056 Other refund conditions are not represented in this matrix\056\056 Check your prediction)
>>
