/Alt (VISUAL LAB 21B \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 A limit must act before the collector fills\056 A hostile program attempts to emit 10 MiB\056 Both designs promise a 64 KiB returned transcript\056 The collector can hold only 1 MiB\073 compare when each cap is enforced\056\056 10 MiB stream\073 64 KiB return cap\073 1 MiB collector limit\056\056 Cap during capture\056 Count bytes as each stream chunk arrives\056 At 64 KiB\054 stop capture and signal limit\056 Terminate controlled execution\073 bound cleanup\056 Captured output stays within 64 KiB\073 report output limit\056 Truncate after capture\056 Append all emitted bytes to the collector\056 Cross 1 MiB before the program completes\056 Final truncation never protects the buffer\056 Collector limit is exceeded before any final 64 KiB slice\056 Both designs advertise the same final transcript size\056\056 Only the left design enforces the bound while bytes arrive\056\056 Artifact and scratch quotas remain separate from the stdout limit\056\056 PREDICT\056 Would increasing the final truncation strictness to 32 KiB repair the right path\077\056 Enforce resource bounds during consumption\054 not after it\056\056 Constructed sizes\054 not measured performance\056 The left provider enforces chunk accounting and termination\073 this example isolates output collection\056\056 Check your prediction)
>>
endobj
