/Alt (VISUAL LAB 22B \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 Which audit claims do these receipts support\077\056 A reviewer inspects three claims about C\0557\056 The receipts are deliberately narrow\072 a live\055delete acknowledgement\054 a writer\055controlled hash\055chain check\054 and a protected external checkpoint digest\056\056 CLAIMS\056 PASSAGES\056 C1\056 C\0557 was removed from the live state store\056\056 S1\056 Live\055state receipt\072 C\0557 delete committed at 14\07203\073 1 row removed\056\056 C2\056 C\0557 was erased immediately from every backup\056\056 S2\056 Local audit chain verifies\073 writer can replace every event and hash\056\056 C3\056 The export matches the externally retained digest\056\056 S3\056 Protected checkpoint\072 export digest 7ac\073 recomputed export digest 7ac\056\056 SUPPORTS\056 INSUFFICIENT\056 SUPPORTS\056 Scope every assurance to the copy\054 event and trust boundary its evidence covers\056\056 The live receipt supports one specific store deletion\056\056 A local hash check says nothing about backup deletion\056\056 An independently protected digest helps detect later rewriting of this export\056\056 PREDICT\056 Does the third receipt prove every original audit event was truthful\077\056 Audit integrity and operational truth require different evidence\056\056 Fictional receipts\073 digest values are abbreviated\056 The external anchor is outside the writer\047s control\073 its protection is an explicit assumption\056\056 Check your prediction)
>>
