/Alt (VISUAL LAB 25A \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 A perfect score can still miss the evidence gate\056 These constructed samples contain independent binary case outcomes\054 not repeated runs of the same prompt\056 A predeclared gate requires the lower end of a two\055sided 95\045 Wilson interval to reach 95\045\056\056 0\045\056 25\045\056 50\045\056 75\045\056 100\045\056 45 of 45 cases\056 Count\072 45 \057 45\056 100\0560\045 \13392\0561\045\054 100\0560\045\135\056 72 of 72 cases\056 Count\072 72 \057 72\056 100\0560\045 \13394\0569\045\054 100\0560\045\135\056 73 of 73 cases\056 Count\072 73 \057 73\056 100\0560\045 \13395\0560\045\054 100\0560\045\135\056 190 of 200 cases\056 Count\072 190 \057 200\056 95\0560\045 \13391\0560\045\054 97\0563\045\135\056 Dashed gate\072 95\045\056 Two\055sided Wilson\054 z \075 1\05696\073 independently checked by score\055test quadratic roots\056\056 All four intervals use the same 0\055100\045 probability scale\056\056 Perfect results with 72 cases still miss the 95\045 lower\055bound floor\056\056 At 73 perfect cases\054 the lower bound just crosses that exact gate\056\056 PREDICT\056 Does 190 successes in 200 cases pass merely because the point estimate is 95\045\077\056 Plan sample size for the bound your gate actually uses\056\056 Constructed independent binary cases\073 nominal coverage assumes this sampling model\056 Repeated or related cases require appropriate clustering\054 not this naive calculation\056\056 Check your prediction)
>>
endobj
