/Alt (VISUAL LAB 25B \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 A judge can agree often and miss dangerous errors\056 The chapter\047s constructed 100\055answer calibration set contains 70 human\055labeled faithful answers and 30 unfaithful answers\056 Every bar counts answers in one mutually exclusive human\057judge outcome\056\056 0\056 64 answers\056 Faithful \057 judge pass\056 64 answers\056 Faithful \057 judge fail\056 6 answers\056 Unfaithful \057 judge pass\056 9 answers\056 Unfaithful \057 judge fail\056 21 answers\056 64 \053 21 \075 85 agreements\073 9 of 30 unfaithful answers are falsely accepted\056\056 The four bars sum to all 100 answers\056\056 Agreement is 85\045\054 but the false\055acceptance denominator is only 30\056\056 Nine false accepts yield a 30\045 error rate among unfaithful answers\056\056 PREDICT\056 Would 85\045 agreement alone justify using this judge as a high\055risk release gate\077\056 Judge agreement does not substitute for inspecting critical errors\056\056 Constructed counts\054 not experimental measurements\073 expert labels are the reviewed reference for this example\056 No universal acceptance threshold is implied\056\056 Check your prediction)
