/Alt (VISUAL LAB 25C \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 Swap the display order before trusting the winner\056 A ShopAssist judge compares fixed replies R and S under one rubric\056 In one constructed trial R appears first\073 in the other S appears first\056 Each trial uses a fresh stochastic judgment\056\056 CLAIMS\056 PASSAGES\056 C1\056 The same reply won both presentations\056\056 S1\056 Pair audit\072 R won the R\057S presentation\073 S won the S\057R presentation\056\056 C2\056 The first displayed reply won in both trials\056\056 S2\056 Verdict log\072 the first slot was selected in both presentations\056\056 C3\056 Display position alone caused the winner to change\056\056 S3\056 Only one stochastic judgment was collected for each display order\056\056 CONFLICTS\056 SUPPORTS\056 INSUFFICIENT\056 Order consistency failed\073 neither a sole cause nor a best reply is established\056\056 Map verdicts back to reply identities\054 not only first or second labels\056\056 The visible pair is inconsistent about which content is better\056\056 One stochastic trial per order cannot isolate position as the only cause\056\056 PREDICT\056 Can the original R\055first verdict alone establish that R is the better reply\077\056 Test judge consistency under harmless presentation changes\056\056 Constructed pair\073 reply content and rubric stay fixed\056 Stochastic judgment remains uncontrolled\054 and neither reply\047s true quality is established\056\056 Check your prediction\056 R25 \057 Zheng et al\056\072 LLM judge position bias)
>>
