/Alt (VISUAL LAB 29C \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 Save the next obligation with the state\056 AegisOps saves INC\05593 after gathering evidence\054 then must schedule hypothesis work\056 Compare a crash at the same point\072 after committing local state but before queue publication\056\056 INC\05593\072 evidence ready\073 hypothesis step must be scheduled\056 Separate state and send\056 Commit state\072 ready for hypothesis\056 Crash before publishing queue message\056 Restart\072 no durable dispatch record\056 Continuation can be lost without a separate repair scan\056\056 State plus outbox\056 Commit state \053 event H\05593 atomically\056 Crash before publishing queue message\056 Relay recovers H\05593 and publishes it\056 Durable scheduling obligation survives\073 duplicates possible\056\056 Both traces lose the worker before any queue publication\056\056 The right transaction stores the pending message alongside the state\056\056 A relay repairs delivery\073 the consumer still deduplicates event H\05593\056\056 PREDICT\056 If the relay publishes H\05593 and crashes before marking it sent\054 what must the consumer tolerate\077\056 Commit the next scheduling obligation with progress\054 then make its delivery safe to repeat\056\056 Fictional crash traces\073 the left design has no repair scan\056 The right relay eventually runs\073 consumer deduplication remains necessary\056\056 Check your prediction\056 R29 \057 AWS\072 Transactional outbox pattern)
>>
