/Alt (VISUAL LAB 30C \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 A finished request gives up its place\056 A constructed decoder has two request slots\056 A and B are active\073 C is eligible and prepared to enter\056 B needs two more steps and A needs four\056 Track only membership\056\056 Boundary 0\056 A and B continue\073 C waits\056 slot 1\056 A\072 4 steps left\056 slot 2\056 B\072 2 steps left\056 waiting\056 C\072 3 steps needed\056 Boundary 2\056 B finishes\073 C takes free slot\056 slot 1\056 A\072 2 steps left\056 slot 2\056 C\072 3 steps left\056 waiting\056 none\056 Boundary 4\056 A finishes\073 C continues\056 slot 1\056 empty\056 slot 2\056 C\072 1 step left\056 waiting\056 none\056 A long request does not force a finished request to keep its slot\056\056 Green edge \075 changed field\073 gray \075 retained field\056\056 At boundary 2\054 A is still running but B has left\056\056 C enters the available slot before A finishes\056\056 At boundary 4\054 C has completed two of its three required steps\056\056 PREDICT\056 Must C wait until boundary 4 solely because A and B entered the earlier batch together\077\056 Continuous batching changes the active roster as requests become ready or finish\056\056 Constructed two\055slot scheduler\073 each active request advances one step per iteration\056 C is prefilled\073 memory\054 prefill scheduling and timing are omitted\056\056 Check your prediction\056 R30 \057 ORCA\072 Iteration\055level scheduling)
