/Alt (VISUAL LAB 31C \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 A decision record carries its limits\056 ShopAssist chose fictional runtime F\0552 for its refund workflow\056 Inspect three claims about the accepted decision against separate excerpts from the same original ADR\0557\056\056 CLAIMS\056 PASSAGES\056 C1\056 F\0552 was chosen to meet the long approval\055wait requirement\056\056 D1\056 ADR\0557 accepted\072 choose F\0552 for refunds needing approval waits of two hours\056\056 C2\056 Choosing F\0552 adds no operating responsibility\056\056 D2\056 ADR\0557 consequence\072 the team must operate and restore the checkpoint database\056\056 C3\056 F\0552 is suitable for every future agent workload\056\056 D3\056 ADR\0557 scope\072 one\055region ShopAssist refunds\056 Revisit if lifecycle needs change\056\056 SUPPORTS\056 CONFLICTS\056 INSUFFICIENT\056 The record explains the choice and its cost\073 it cannot establish universal fitness\056\056 D1 explains why the team selected F\0552 for this workload\056\056 D2 records a consequence that a feature comparison might hide\056\056 D3 limits the decision to a stated context and names a revisit condition\056\056 PREDICT\056 Does accepted status in ADR\0557 prove that a waiting refund actually survives a database restore\077\056 Preserve the reason and consequences of a framework choice alongside the evidence that tests it\056\056 Fictional ADR excerpts\054 runtime and requirement\073 accepted status is not a benchmark\054 migration result or business\055action approval\056\056 Check your prediction\056 R31 \057 Nygard\072 Architecture decision records)
>>
