/Alt (VISUAL LAB 32A \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 Retransmission is not new evidence\056 Two AegisOps branches return evidence E\05517\056 The reducer treats each evidence identity as immutable\054 so identical retransmission and conflicting content must behave differently\056\056 Step 1 \055 first fact\056 Accept E\05517\072 p95 \075 620 ms\056 E\05517\056 p95 \075 620 ms\056 entry count\056 1\056 merge outcome\056 accepted\056 Step 2 \055 repeat\056 E\05517 again\072 p95 \075 620 ms\056 E\05517\056 p95 \075 620 ms\056 entry count\056 1\056 merge outcome\056 unchanged\056 Step 3 \055 conflict\056 E\05517 offered as 250 ms\056 E\05517\056 p95 \075 620 ms\056 entry count\056 1\056 merge outcome\056 rejected\072 ID conflict\056 An accepted evidence ID never silently changes its content\056\056 Green edge \075 changed field\073 gray \075 retained field\056\056 The second arrival does not increase the ledger size\056\056 The conflicting third update cannot replace E\05517\056\056 A genuine correction needs a new version with a supersession link\056\056 PREDICT\056 If the child subgraph returns its received E\05517 plus E\05517 again\054 how many entries should remain\077\056 Define merge semantics from evidence meaning before parallelizing nodes\056\056 Fictional state\073 the reducer is atomic for each merge\056 The shown merge outcome is explanatory instrumentation\056\056 Check your prediction)
>>
