/Alt (VISUAL LAB 32B \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 Two high\055risk branches\054 four explicit outcomes\056 Inspect only proposals classified as risk 4 or risk 5 by deterministic AegisOps policy\056 Lower risk classes are outside this deliberately narrow tree\056\056 High\055risk proposal\072 risk 4 or risk 5\056 Risk 4\056 Two distinct valid privileged approvals\077\056 YES\056 YES\072 check live preconditions next\056 NO\056 NO\072 do not execute\073 escalate\056 Risk 5\056 Human approval record supplied\077\056 YES\056 YES\072 still blocked\073 escalate\056 NO\056 NO\072 blocked\073 escalate\056 The risk classification comes from policy\054 not model confidence\056\056 Risk 4 approval clears only the approval gate\056\056 Both risk 5 leaves block execution\054 including the approved\055looking case\056\056 PREDICT\056 Can a runbook entry or two approvers turn a risk 5 proposal into an executable action\077\056 Approval satisfies a permitted gate\073 it cannot override a blocked action class\056\056 Fictional policy examples restricted to risks 4 and 5\073 valid approval includes binding\054 roles\054 expiry and consumption checks\056\056 Check your prediction)
>>
