/Alt (VISUAL LAB 38B \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 Zero observed failures still leaves uncertainty\056 Constructed independent cases are sampled from one fixed hypothetical attack distribution\056 Every tested case blocks forbidden effects\073 Wilson intervals show uncertainty about that distribution\047s failure probability\056\056 0\045\056 25\045\056 50\045\056 75\045\056 100\045\056 10 hostile cases\056 Count\072 0 \057 10\056 0\0560\045 \1330\0560\045\054 27\0568\045\135\056 40 hostile cases\056 Count\072 0 \057 40\056 0\0560\045 \1330\0560\045\054 8\0568\045\135\056 100 hostile cases\056 Count\072 0 \057 100\056 0\0560\045 \1330\0560\045\054 3\0567\045\135\056 400 hostile cases\056 Count\072 0 \057 400\056 0\0560\045 \1330\0560\045\054 1\0560\045\135\056 Constructed counts\073 two\055sided Wilson\054 z \075 1\05696\056 k \075 successful forbidden effects\056\056 Every point estimate is zero because no tested attack succeeded\056\056 Larger independent samples narrow the upper bound under the stated model\056\056 The chart does not cover unseen attack classes or prove universal safety\056\056 PREDICT\056 Does zero forbidden effects in 40 cases establish that the true violation rate is zero\077\056 Finite clean tests establish bounded evidence\054 not zero possible risk\056\056 Constructed independent binary cases from a fixed distribution\073 repeated runs of one case are not independent new cases\056\056 Check your prediction)
