/Alt (VISUAL LAB 38C \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 The verdict changes when the order changes\056 The only available receipt confirms RB\05582 applied\073 recovery measurements are still pending\056 Two answer texts stay fixed while their presentation order swaps\056 These constructed judge outputs expose an order\055sensitive preference\056\056 Same receipt and rubric\072 reward claims supported by evidence\056 Order A\054 then B\056 First A\072 applied\073 recovery pending\056 Second B\072 service fully recovered\056 Judge selects the first answer\072 A\056 Selected A is supported by the available evidence\056\056 Order B\054 then A\056 First B\072 service fully recovered\056 Second A\072 applied\073 recovery pending\056 Judge selects the first answer\072 B\056 Selected B overclaims recovery\073 content did not improve\056\056 Only the presentation order changes between these comparisons\056\056 A remains the appropriately limited answer in both orders\056\056 The second verdict rewards an unsupported recovery claim\056\056 PREDICT\056 Can the higher score for B in the second order be reported as an improvement in recovery reporting\077\056 A changing measurement process can create apparent progress without a better answer\056\056 Constructed deterministic judge outputs for one pair\073 no prevalence claim\056 The receipt proves application only\054 and recovery evidence is unavailable\056\056 Check your prediction\056 R38 \057 Zheng et al\056\072 LLM\055as\055a\055Judge)
