/Alt (VISUAL LAB 39C \057 SEE \267 TRACE \267 PREDICT\056 Ninety percent alone misses the refund gate\056 Track A requires observed conversation success of at least 90\045 and a two\055sided 95\045 Wilson lower bound of at least 85\045\056 Compare four alternative constructed results for 120 independent cases\056\056 0\045\056 25\045\056 50\045\056 75\045\056 100\045\056 108 of 120 successful\056 Count\072 108 \057 120\056 90\0560\045 \13383\0563\045\054 94\0562\045\135\056 109 of 120 successful\056 Count\072 109 \057 120\056 90\0568\045 \13384\0563\045\054 94\0568\045\135\056 110 of 120 successful\056 Count\072 110 \057 120\056 91\0567\045 \13385\0563\045\054 95\0564\045\135\056 111 of 120 successful\056 Count\072 111 \057 120\056 92\0565\045 \13386\0564\045\054 96\0560\045\135\056 Dashed gate\072 85\045\056 Constructed counts\073 k \075 successful conversations\056 Two\055sided Wilson\054 z \075 1\05696\056\056 All four point estimates reach the separate 90\045 requirement\056\056 The 85\045 line tests the lower endpoint\054 not the point estimate\056\056 Only 110 and 111 successes put that lower endpoint above 85\045\056\056 PREDICT\056 Does 109 successful conversations pass both statistical requirements\054 and would 110 override an unauthorized refund\077\056 Check the point estimate and uncertainty requirement separately\054 then apply every hard safety gate\056\056 Constructed independent binary cases from one fixed hypothetical population\073 one fixed analysis\056 Alternative rows are not repeated peeks during a sequential test\056\056 Check your prediction\056 R39 \057 NIST\072 Wilson proportion intervals)
>>
